      "content": "That's a bit too bare-bones. I get that we want brevity, but if a junior SRE comes across this, they might struggle if they don't have the context or if they hit a hiccup. \n\nCan you expand it a bit? Make it more of a proper \"guide\"—maybe include some brief context for each command, what they should expect to see, and some basic prerequisites. Just keep it practical. Avoid the fluff, but I don't want it to look like a tiny snippet. Our audit metric is watching, so let's make sure it looks substantial enough to pass the completeness check without being annoying.",
