      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a step in the right direction. It's still looking a little thin for a professional doc, though. Usually, a \"Quick Start\" includes a bit more about the environment requirements, maybe a troubleshooting section for common errors, and some details on what the CLI actually does.\n\nThe audit team is a bit strict about the completeness score being too low for anything that's supposed to be official documentation. If it's too short, it just gets flagged. Could you flesh this out into a more comprehensive document? Include things like prerequisites, what to check after running each command, and a few potential error scenarios. Again, just make it actually useful/professional and don't just add junk for the sake of it, but we definitely need more substance here.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
